; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Musical Words
; CATEGORY: Music & Sound
; LEVEL:    Beginner
; TAGS:     property list, words, sound, letters
; SUMMARY:  Uses a property list to turn note names into frequencies and plays English words spelled only with the letters A to G.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   Musicians name notes with the letters A B C D E F G. Some English
;   words use only those letters, like CABBAGE, FACE and BADGE, so
;   you can play them! The program looks up each letter in a property
;   list, plays it, and writes the word in big letters as it goes.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run with the sound on. Add your own words to the list at
;   the bottom. Letters that are not notes are skipped with a short
;   rest, so any word works, but the A to G words sound the best.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * PPROP stores a value under a name in a property list
;   * GPROP looks the value up again; an unknown name gives the empty list
;   * a word is a sequence of letters that FOREACH can walk through
;   * SOUND with a frequency of 0 makes a silent rest
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Find more A to G words: BEADED, DECADE, CAFE, EGG, BAGGAGE.
;   * Make the notes longer by changing the 250 in PLAYLETTER.
;   * Store the notes one octave higher by doubling every number.
; ============================================================

; One property list called "notes holds a frequency for each letter.
pprop "notes "a 440
pprop "notes "b 494
pprop "notes "c 262
pprop "notes "d 294
pprop "notes "e 330
pprop "notes "f 349
pprop "notes "g 392

; Play one letter. GPROP outputs the empty list when the letter is
; not in the property list, so we check with EMPTYP before playing.
to playletter :ch
  localmake "freq gprop "notes lowercase :ch
  ifelse emptyp :freq [sound [0 250]] [sound (list :freq 250)]
end

; Write the word one letter at a time, playing each letter as it
; appears, so the eyes and ears follow along together.
to playword :w :y
  penup setxy -200 :y pendown
  foreach :w [
    label ?
    playletter ?
    penup setx xcor + 45 pendown
  ]
  sound [0 400]   ; a breath between words
end

clearscreen
hideturtle
setbackground [30 30 60]
setlabelheight 40
make "words [cabbage face badge deaf bead egg]
make "y 220
foreach :words [
  setpencolor 1 + remainder # 15
  playword uppercase ? :y
  make "y :y - 80
]
